            "derivation": "Returning the supplied heights unchanged asserts x=y at all three intersections. For instance the height 2.5 intersects the curve near x=6.3, not x=2.5.",
            "misconception": "Copy each given y value directly as its x coordinate, implicitly replacing the square-root graph by the identity correspondence."
